<br>

Data type: The kind of data a variable can store (like numbers, text, or true/false).
<br>
Variable: A named place in memory used to store a value that can change while the program runs.
<br>

int age = 20;          // integer variable
double price = 9.99;   // decimal number
string name = "Alex";  // text
bool isStudent = true; // true/false
<br>
int, double, string, bool = data types
variable name = identifier
= = assignment operator
value = data stored in the variable
